01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
Phantom Thread is a 2017 psychological period drama film
written and directed by Paul Thomas Anderson.

11
01:08:05,714 --> 01:08:11,714
It stars Daniel Day-Lewis, Vicky Krieps, and Lesley Manville, and follows a haute
couture dressmaker in 1950s London who takes a young waitress as his muse.

12
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
It is Anderson's first film shot outside the United States, with principal
photography beginning in January 2017 in Lythe, England.

13
01:20:28,571 --> 01:20:34,571
It is also Anderson's second collaboration with Day-Lewis, after There Will Be Blood
(2007), and his fourth collaboration with composer Jonny Greenwood.

14
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Phantom Thread premiered in New York City on December 11, 2017, and was
theatrically released in the United States two weeks later.

15
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
It received acclaim for its acting, screenplay, direction,
musical score, costume design, and production values.

16
01:39:02,857 --> 01:39:08,857
The National Board of Review chose it as one of the top ten films of 2017, and
it is widely considered one of the best films of the 2010s.

17
01:45:14,285 --> 01:45:20,285
At the 90th Academy Awards, the film was nominated for Best Picture, Best Director, Best Actor (Day-Lewis),
Best Supporting Actress (Manville), and Best Original Score; it won for Best Costume Design.

18
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
It also earned four nominations at the 71st British Academy Film Awards, winning
for Best Costume Design, and received two Golden Globe nominations.

19
01:57:37,142 --> 01:57:43,142
The film explores themes of london, england, husband wife
relationship, obsession, dressmaker, fashion designer.

20
02:03:48,571 --> 02:03:54,571
The tone is emotional.
